.Dd August 2, 2026
.Dt GITHUB-TOKEN-BROKER-CONFIG 5
.Os
.\" -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Sh NAME
.Nm github-token-broker-config
.Nd configuration file format for github-token-broker
.\" -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr github-token-broker 8
reads one JSON file, named on the command line as an absolute path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
github-token-broker --config /etc/github-token-broker/config.json
.Ed
.Pp
The file names the App to mint as, where requests are accepted, and which
repositories may be minted for.
Nothing else decides any of those, and no client can influence them: an
environment variable cannot add a listener or reach a repository this document
omits.
The log level is the one setting that lives outside; see
.Xr github-token-broker 8 .
.Pp
The document is read once at startup, so a change takes effect on restart.
.Pp
An unrecognized member anywhere in the document fails startup, so a misspelled
security-sensitive key is refused rather than silently ignored.
Comments and trailing commas are not accepted either; this is strict JSON.
.\" -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Sh TOP-LEVEL SETTINGS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic app_id
Required.
The App's numeric identity, from its registration.
Signed into every JWT as
.Ql iss .
Must be positive.
.It Ic installation_id
Required.
Which installation of that App to mint against, the number at the end of the
installation's settings URL.
Must be positive.
An entry under
.Ic repositories
may name a different one; this is what the rest take.
See
.Sx Installations .
.It Ic private_key_path
Required.
Absolute path to the App's PEM private key.
Re-read on every mint, so replacing the file rotates the key with no restart.
.It Ic listen
Required.
Where requests are accepted.
See
.Sx LISTEN .
.It Ic repositories
Required.
The allowlist, and the permission ceiling for each entry.
See
.Sx REPOSITORIES .
.It Ic github_host
Defaults to
.Ql github.com ,
which is the only accepted value today.
The setting exists so that a second host becomes a configuration change rather
than a code change.
.It Ic api_url
Defaults to
.Ql https://api.github.com .
Must be
.Ql https ,
or
.Ql http
against loopback only.
A query or fragment is refused.
It exists to point the broker at a fake in a test, which is why plaintext is
tolerated there and nowhere else.
This is not GitHub Enterprise support.
.It Ic token_refresh_margin_seconds
Defaults to
.Ql 300 .
How much life a cached token must have left to be reused.
Between 30 and 1800: an installation token lives one hour, so a margin
approaching that would make every token stale on arrival.
.El
.\" -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Sh REPOSITORIES
.Ic repositories
is the whole of what may be minted.
A client names one repository and receives a token for it.
It cannot reach a repository absent from this list, and cannot influence the
permissions attached to one that is present.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "repositories": {
    "example-owner/example-repo": {
      "permissions": {
        "contents": "write",
        "pull_requests": "write",
        "actions": "read"
      }
    },
    "example-owner/another-repo": {
      "permissions": { "contents": "read" }
    }
  }
}
.Ed
.Pp
Each key names a repository in
.Ar OWNER Ns / Ns Ar REPOSITORY
form, spelled the way GitHub spells it and without a
.Pa .git
suffix.
At least one repository is required, and each entry must declare at least one
permission.
.Pp
Matching ignores case, as GitHub's does.
Two entries differing only in case would collapse onto one identity, so the
pair is refused.
This applies to the repository key alone; the permission names and levels under
it are matched exactly.
.Pp
A repository absent from the list is refused with the same status and message
as every other refusal, so a caller cannot use error text to discover what is
here.
.\"
.Ss Permissions are a ceiling
The map under a repository is exactly what the broker asks GitHub for, and a
grant exceeding it is refused rather than returned.
A token therefore never carries more authority than is written here, even where
the installation would allow more.
.Pp
Supported permissions, each at
.Ql read
or
.Ql write :
.Ql metadata ,
.Ql contents ,
.Ql pull_requests ,
.Ql issues ,
.Ql actions ,
.Ql checks ,
.Ql statuses .
A name outside this set fails validation rather than reaching GitHub.
.Pp
.Ql Contents
and
.Ql Read
are therefore refused as unsupported.
.Pp
GitHub reports
.Ql metadata: read
on every installation token whether or not it was asked for, so that one grant
is tolerated in a response even when configuration omits it.
.Pp
Which of these to grant is a deployment question; see SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
in
.Xr github-token-broker 8 .
.Pp
.Ql workflows
is refused at any level, with a diagnostic distinct from an unsupported name:
authority over workflow files is outside this design.
.Pp
Narrowing an entry takes effect on the next mint rather than the next restart.
See CACHE in
.Xr github-token-broker 8 .
.\"
.Ss Installations
An entry may carry its own
.Ic installation_id ,
which is how a repository outside the App owner's account is served: its owner
installs the same App, and that installation's number goes here.
The top-level value serves every entry that omits one.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "installation_id": 789012,
  "repositories": {
    "example-owner/example-repo": {
      "permissions": { "contents": "write" }
    },
    "other-owner/their-repo": {
      "installation_id": 345678,
      "permissions": { "contents": "write", "pull_requests": "write" }
    }
  }
}
.Ed
.Pp
One App and one private key throughout: an installation is an address, and the
key is the credential that addresses it.
A rejected App JWT therefore still discards every cached grant.
.Pp
Whether an installation covers the repository listed against it is settled at
the first mint, the broker reaching GitHub for nothing else.
A mismatch answers as a missing installation; see
.Xr github-token-broker 8 .
.\" -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Sh LISTEN
.Ic listen
must configure
.Ic unix_socket ,
which is one object per transport rather than a flat set of keys, so a second
transport arrives beside it.
.Pp
Authorization is filesystem access, so there is no shared secret to distribute,
rotate, or leak, and nothing bound that another host could reach.
A caller in a container reaches the socket by bind-mounting it; see
.Xr github-token 1 .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "app_id": 123456,
  "installation_id": 789012,
  "private_key_path": "/etc/github-token-broker/app.pem",
  "listen": {
    "unix_socket": {
      "path": "/run/github-token-broker/broker.sock",
      "mode": "0600"
    }
  },
  "repositories": {
    "example-owner/example-repo": {
      "permissions": {
        "contents": "write",
        "pull_requests": "write"
      }
    }
  }
}
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic unix_socket.path
Required.
Absolute path to bind.
Must fit the platform's
.Vt sockaddr_un
limit, which is 104 bytes on macOS and 108 on Linux.
.It Ic unix_socket.mode
Defaults to
.Ql 0600 .
Three octal digits, optionally with a leading zero, written as a JSON string.
.El
.Pp
Connecting needs write permission on the socket, so this mode is who may mint.
A mode granting write to others is refused, as is one that withholds read and
write from the owner.
The setuid, setgid, and sticky bits are not accepted here.
.Pp
Sharing with a group is
.Ql 0660
plus group ownership from the service unit.
The socket's directory is the outer half of the same control; see
.Xr github-token-broker 8 .
.\" -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It The App private key
A PEM RSA private key, readable only by the account the broker runs as.
.Ic private_key_path
names it by path rather than value, so this document carries no secret and can
be read by anyone who needs to understand the deployment.
.Pp
It is read at startup, so an unreadable one fails the broker with its own exit
status rather than surfacing at the first mint.
Where it may live, and why not in a container, is in
.Xr github-token-broker 8 .
.El
.\" -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
A document that fails validation is reported on standard error and the broker
exits 78 without listening.
The message names the member at fault and never echoes a secret.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ github-token-broker --config /etc/github-token-broker/config.json
configuration error: The token_refresh_margin_seconds value must be
between 30 and 1800.
.Ed
